                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sharing Our Story"
              }
            ],
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "type": "richText",
            "role": "body",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This year, we've made an impact on Toronto's creative industry by inspiring interest in print media and indie magazines in the very digital age we're living in. "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "href": "https://torontolife.com/culture/toronto-indie-magazines/",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "emphasis",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Toronto Life"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "emphasis",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "writes \"Lore is arguably the trailblazer that kicked off this new wave of the indie magazine trend\". The team also gave a guest lecture at Toronto Metropolitan University for the course CRI/FCD 760: Diversity in the Creative Industries, sharing how we create, collaborate, and how we got started with the magazine. Recently, we just had the launch of our 4th issue, The Club Issue, and it was a great experience to celebrate our community and the achievements of the collaborators. Overall, Lore has been a very rewarding project to be apart of and something I'm proud to share with the community. "
              }
            ]
          }
